{"id": "EUVD-2026-86770", "enisaUuid": "0feab6cc-30b1-3b09-b253-879dd49b874d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naccel/ivpu: Validate firmware log buffer metadata\n\nThe tracing log headers parsed by fw_log_print_buffer() reside in\nDMA-shared BOs that the NPU firmware can write to.\n\nfw_log_from_bo() validated log->header_size and log->size, but\nfw_log_print_buffer() re-read those same fields from shared memory\nafterwards, allowing a TOCTOU where firmware changes them between the\ncheck and the use, and making the host dereference out-of-bounds\naddresses while printing logs.\n\nSnapshot the validated values once with READ_ONCE() and pass them down\nexplicitly in a new struct ivpu_fw_log_desc instead of re-reading them\nfrom the shared struct.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:53:35", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/07d4190d75021c38b7994045179aa29131634d4f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ec3d6972f1440fae6c8dadd1859892775208759", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/40868f80a89199630b03d4457876f9a1feba0660", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b1555f63ee1a680f280bc18e8dac416f250e2ec3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0724afc55c77c36c7feb9a7264b02aa7593c5c2d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97916", "GHSA-9698-pw26-h6mc"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c409353-e966-3b0b-940b-87af7034e45b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "13f9aa94-a784-3566-86e2-51fa65c889fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "19d06507-2b86-3c74-85d4-b52e3e20ceb4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2f9beaf4-1710-3853-ae8f-7adb13bbc034", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d4e4257afa6ed5205eda993180401fc2c20e4b60 <b1555f63ee1a680f280bc18e8dac416f250e2ec3"}, {"id": "43d9add7-8aba-3ea6-816f-a2e89d09d543", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "51afbbb6-ce1d-3157-92de-d3921154800a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d4e4257afa6ed5205eda993180401fc2c20e4b60 <40868f80a89199630b03d4457876f9a1feba0660"}, {"id": "ad838e2f-8c43-312f-a7e5-f7c26dbaa57c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d4e4257afa6ed5205eda993180401fc2c20e4b60 <8ec3d6972f1440fae6c8dadd1859892775208759"}, {"id": "ae329ed6-2bd4-3fb4-9e36-1ced508c9ade", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d4e4257afa6ed5205eda993180401fc2c20e4b60 <07d4190d75021c38b7994045179aa29131634d4f"}, {"id": "b46bcbec-2b3e-3906-8b4f-48cdc6c4d4ba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d4e4257afa6ed5205eda993180401fc2c20e4b60 <0724afc55c77c36c7feb9a7264b02aa7593c5c2d"}, {"id": "b7adf258-f59c-3512-b2cf-449091b36e02", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "cc4ce3bd-28b1-31b4-915a-113fc49f5992", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "fcc86733-0191-35d3-a8d7-e778562b098a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5ad396e2-88c2-352f-b25a-0867957d2ee4", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}